Z||000000||JohnF||11-08-2001||04:01 PM||||The infamous dew wipes, again!<P>True or false - <P>OUTER dew wipes can be replaced by removing INNER door panel only.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-08-2001||04:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnF:<BR><B>The infamous dew wipes, again!<P>True or false - <P>OUTER dew wipes can be replaced by removing INNER door panel only.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And the inner wipes so you can pull the glass in a little to access the screws.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||JSocha||11-08-2001||04:48 PM||||Just make sure you get and/or have the DEW STRIP tool from Rodney Dickman.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>And make sure you have a few strips of ELECTRICAL TAPE to hang the two screws on each door to get them in position to put them back in again versus taping them to the tool.  Much quicker.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||11-08-2001||06:02 PM||||Hey!  Thanks for the answers.  <P>For the 1st time I am replacing a bad wiper without having to replace outer skin.  <P>Just wanted to make sure before I started that the outer skin didn't have to be removed.<P>BTW - Dew wipe was still available from my local Pontiac dealer.  ||||reg||12
